# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for check-resolverd-tsan.
#
# Only for races TSan cannot see the synchronisation of: uninstrumented
# third-party code. Each entry is filed with its report in
# CLAUDE-resolverd-cache.md ("TSan findings"). Never add an entry for
# project code — fix the race instead.
#
# OpenSSL >= 3.3 looks up algorithm names in its lock-free (RCU) hashtable
# (ossl_ht_get, from EVP_PKEY_fromdata / EVP fetch in verify_ecdsa_p256 /
# verify_ed25519). libcrypto is not built with -fsanitize=thread, so the RCU
# publication is invisible to TSan and every concurrent DNSSEC verify is
# reported as a race on the hashtable's key buffer.
race:ossl_ht_get
#
# Same race when libcrypto has no symbols (the CI runner): the frames inside
# libcrypto print as <null>, so the name above cannot match and the report
# halted resolverd mid-run (CI #43821003735). Suppress interceptor reports
# (memcmp/memcpy) made from inside libcrypto itself; a race in project code
# is still reported, since its accesses are not made from libcrypto.
called_from_lib:libcrypto.so
